{
  "form": "mutation_list",
  "rationale": "Three execute items were already implemented outside the swarm-manager flow and only the heartbeat/skill end-to-end coverage in the test chore remains.",
  "mutations": [
    {
      "id": "m1",
      "op": "archive_item",
      "target": "execute/swarm-manager-pending-questions-priority-sort",
      "rationale": "Implemented: pending_questions.go sorts via backlogrank (depth + priority + recency + unblocking boost) and the CLI subcommand `backlog pending-questions` with --source/--limit/--initiative/--json is wired in cmd_backlog.go and domains/backlog/register.go. The plan's deliverables match the current code."
    },
    {
      "id": "m2",
      "op": "archive_item",
      "target": "execute/workshop-decision-prep-agent",
      "rationale": "Implemented: scenarios/prompt-manager/store/teams/director-swarm/members/workshop-decision-prep/ contains heartbeat.json (cron `0 */3 * * *`, enabled), HEARTBEAT.md (read prior handoff, recompute SHA-256 over topic+text+context+options, drop stale/answered briefs, early-return at 15 valid briefs, enrich up to 20, clarification feed-forward), RESPONSIBILITIES.md, and the initial last-handoff.md. Matches the planned member contract."
    },
    {
      "id": "m3",
      "op": "archive_item",
      "target": "execute/workshop-decision-sync-skill",
      "rationale": "Implemented: scenarios/prompt-manager/store/skills/packs/core/workshop-decision-sync/ has skill.json (mode=practice, swarm-manager/decisions tags) and SKILL.md covering staged-handoff intake, freshness checks with lazy fallback, focus stack, fetch-patch-save through workshop/save, skip/clarify surfaces, and completion reporting."
    },
    {
      "id": "m4",
      "op": "update_item",
      "target": "chore/workshop-decision-sync-tests",
      "patch": {
        "title": "End-to-end scenario + skill-smoke coverage for workshop-decision-prep heartbeat and sync skill",
        "description": "Remaining test coverage after the three execute items landed.\n\nDone (do NOT redo):\n- Go test (scenarios/swarm-manager/api/internal/backlog/pending_questions_test.go): sorted-by-dependency-depth-and-priority, unblocking-boost-beats-recency, limit + --initiative filter, invalid-query-params, mixed sources.\n- Go test (scenarios/swarm-manager/cli/app_test.go): TestCmdBacklogPendingQuestionsValidation and TestCmdBacklogPendingQuestionsRequestsExpectedEndpoint cover --source/--limit/--initiative flag forwarding and the `/api/v1/backlog/pending-questions` endpoint.\n\nStill to deliver:\n1. Scenario test (test-genie or manual harness): seed swarm-manager with 3 backlog items across 2 initiatives, each with 2 open workshop decisions; run the workshop-decision-prep heartbeat; assert last-handoff.md shape, per-brief content_hash presence, and early-return behavior when the cap is already met. Then mutate one decision's options and re-run, asserting only that one brief is refreshed. Then call POST /api/v1/backlog/{kind}/{name}/workshop/save for one decision (simulating UI answer) and re-run the skill's freshness step, asserting the now-answered decision is dropped.\n2. Skill smoke test: documented manual test plan that invokes the workshop-decision-sync skill with a fully staged handoff and confirms (a) narrative grouping by initiative -> backlog item -> decision, (b) focus-stack behavior when the operator asks a clarifying question mid-decision, and (c) async clarification spawn via `swarm-manager backlog clarify`, with the session continuing past the spawn."
      },
      "rationale": "The Go-side test coverage already exists; rescoping the chore to only the missing scenario heartbeat test and the manual skill smoke test plan prevents duplicate work and keeps the chore relevant."
    }
  ]
}
